00:44:31,901 --> 00:44:34,146
Speaker 1: And they're never going to do any pay-to-wins, ever.

532
00:44:34,868 --> 00:44:38,397
Speaker 1: It's just time grinding, and even not that much of that, really.

533
00:44:38,778 --> 00:44:39,720
Speaker 1: It doesn't matter that much.

534
00:44:40,120 --> 00:44:58,700
Speaker 1: So if you want to play something with a unique concept, with amazing arts and atmosphere to sort of make up for any suffering you have from losing a bunch, or maybe you want to really get good at it and have high skills in quick matches, or maybe you don't want high skills, but you have enough friends.

535
00:44:58,880 --> 00:45:00,023
Speaker 1: You don't need that many friends.

536
00:45:00,063 --> 00:45:03,433
Speaker 1: You just need one friend is enough to play this game.

537
00:45:03,453 --> 00:45:06,160
Speaker 1: You can play 1v1, and that's a full experience.

538
00:45:06,641 --> 00:45:08,244
Speaker 0: And they're really different.

539
00:45:08,485 --> 00:45:10,590
Speaker 0: 1v1 is like a really tense duel.

540
00:45:10,610 --> 00:45:14,820
Speaker 0: You know that feeling we used to get at RIT when you're playing old-school Counter-Strike?

541
00:45:15,201 --> 00:45:20,153
Speaker 0: And there's just one person alive on each team, and that tense, sneaking-around standoff.

542
00:45:20,634 --> 00:45:23,020
Speaker 0: You get that feeling a lot in this game.

543
00:45:23,660 --> 00:45:27,313
Speaker 1: Normally, a 1v1 FPS is just like, "Who sees the other guy

544
00:45:27,353 --> 00:45:28,216
Speaker 1: first?".

545
00:45:28,698 --> 00:45:29,220
Speaker 1: And that's it.

546
00:45:29,500 --> 00:45:36,937
Speaker 1: And so, by adding the cards, the 1v1 actually becomes this wild game of luck and strategy.

547
00:45:37,017 --> 00:45:38,260
Speaker 1: and what cards did you bring.

548
00:45:38,480 --> 00:45:43,211
Speaker 1: And you see how they're trying to play, what character they've chosen.

549
00:45:43,652 --> 00:45:47,340
Speaker 1: Like, if they choose Tiger-Melee-Only-Katana-Guy, right?

550
00:45:47,420 --> 00:45:48,667
Speaker 1: Yes, Tiger with a katana.

551
00:45:48,687 --> 00:45:50,357
Speaker 1: If that doesn't sell the game, I don't know what will.

552
00:45:51,901 --> 00:45:56,733
Speaker 1: If you know they're the Tiger with the katana, you can change your strategy.

553
00:45:57,394 --> 00:45:59,620
Speaker 1: So they're probably doing things to disable your guns.

554
00:46:00,661 --> 00:46:07,419
Speaker 1: You can do things to sort of keep them away from you, or to make yourself move faster, so they can't get within range to use the katana on you.

555
00:46:08,001 --> 00:46:09,587
Speaker 1: And shoot them while you're running away.

556
00:46:09,607 --> 00:46:12,817
Speaker 1: You have to think about that sort of thing in these matches.

557
00:46:16,262 --> 00:46:23,160
Speaker 1: The FPS skill matters significantly enough that I suck, but it's not the only thing that matters.

558
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:29,180
Speaker 1: The other things will get you some kills here and there, and if you combine both, now you're ready for the big leagues.

559
